/* Verse Games: THE WHOLE COUNSEL · Micah chapters 1-5
   Verse text is filled/verified from the KJV by tools/fill-verses.js */
VG.registerBibleChapters("micah", [
{n:1, name:"The Fall of Samaria", seal:{ref:"Micah 1:9",verse:"For her wound is incurable; for it is come unto Judah; he is come unto the gate of my people, even to Jerusalem."}, facts:["Did you know Micah was called 'the Morasthite,' naming him for his hometown Moresheth in the Judean foothills, and he prophesied under three kings: Jotham, Ahaz, and Hezekiah (Micah 1:1)?","Did you know Micah's lament for the towns of Judah plays on their names? He tells Aphrah, which sounds like the Hebrew word for dust, to roll in the dust, and Achzib, which sounds like deception, will be a lie to the kings (Micah 1:10, 14).","Did you know 'Make thee bald, and poll thee' (Micah 1:16) points to the mourning custom of shaving the head in deep grief, and here the grief itself becomes the prophecy, for the children are gone into captivity?"], questions:[
{q:"In whose days did Micah prophesy?", options:["In the days of Jotham, Ahaz, and Hezekiah","In the days of David and Solomon","In the days of Josiah and Zedekiah","In the days of the Babylonian exile"], a:0, ref:"Micah 1:1",verse:"The word of the LORD that came to Micah the Morasthite in the days of Jotham, Ahaz, and Hezekiah, kings of Judah, which he saw concerning Samaria and Jerusalem.", insight:"Three kings, one prophet; God keeps speaking even when thrones change hands."},
{q:"What was Micah called?", options:["Micah the Morasthite","Micah the Gileadite","Micah the Bethlehemite","Micah the son of Imla"], a:0, ref:"Micah 1:1",verse:"The word of the LORD that came to Micah the Morasthite in the days of Jotham, Ahaz, and Hezekiah, kings of Judah, which he saw concerning Samaria and Jerusalem.", insight:"God often raises His messengers in small towns the maps barely notice."},
{q:"Who is called to hear the Lord's case?", options:["All ye people, and the earth, and all that therein is","Only the priests of Jerusalem","Only the kings of Judah","The nations round about alone"], a:0, ref:"Micah 1:2",verse:"Hear, all ye people; hearken, O earth, and all that therein is: and let the Lord GOD be witness against you, the Lord from his holy temple.", insight:"When God brings His case, the whole earth is the courtroom; none may claim they were not called."},
{q:"Who will be witness against them?", options:["The Lord GOD, from his holy temple","The king of Assyria","The elders of Israel","The prophet Micah himself"], a:0, ref:"Micah 1:2",verse:"Hear, all ye people; hearken, O earth, and all that therein is: and let the Lord GOD be witness against you, the Lord from his holy temple.", insight:"The witness is not a man but the Lord from His holy temple; His testimony never needs cross examination."},
{q:"What will the LORD do when He comes forth out of His place?", options:["Come down, and tread upon the high places of the earth","Hide Himself in the temple","Send a famine upon the land","Call the nations to peace"], a:0, ref:"Micah 1:3",verse:"For, behold, the LORD cometh forth out of his place, and will come down, and tread upon the high places of the earth.", insight:"The high places of man's pride are God's footstool; what men exalt, He treads down."},
{q:"What will happen to the mountains under Him?", options:["They shall be molten, and the valleys cleft, as wax before the fire","They shall stand forever unchanged","They shall grow taller than the heavens","They shall flee into the sea"], a:0, ref:"Micah 1:4",verse:"And the mountains shall be molten under him, and the valleys shall be cleft, as wax before the fire, and as the waters that are poured down a steep place.", insight:"Before God's presence, what looks unmovable melts like wax; nothing in creation can resist its Maker."},
{q:"What is named as the transgression of Jacob?", options:["Samaria","Gath","Lachish","Adullam"], a:0, ref:"Micah 1:5",verse:"For the transgression of Jacob is all this, and for the sins of the house of Israel. What is the transgression of Jacob? is it not Samaria? and what are the high places of Judah? are they not Jerusalem?", insight:"God names the sin plainly, with no softening; Samaria's idolatry is called by its right name."},
{q:"What are the high places of Judah?", options:["Jerusalem","Hebron","Bethlehem","Gibeon"], a:0, ref:"Micah 1:5",verse:"For the transgression of Jacob is all this, and for the sins of the house of Israel. What is the transgression of Jacob? is it not Samaria? and what are the high places of Judah? are they not Jerusalem?", insight:"Judgment begins closer to home than we expect; Jerusalem's own high places stand accused."},
{q:"What will Samaria become?", options:["As an heap of the field, and as plantings of a vineyard","A royal city of Assyria","A market for the nations","A garden of the LORD"], a:0, ref:"Micah 1:6",verse:"Therefore I will make Samaria as an heap of the field, and as plantings of a vineyard: and I will pour down the stones thereof into the valley, and I will discover the foundations thereof.", insight:"The proud capital will be reduced to a farm plot; God levels what sin has lifted."},
{q:"What will happen to Samaria's graven images?", options:["They shall be beaten to pieces, and her idols laid desolate","They shall be carried to the temple in Jerusalem","They shall be sold to the merchants","They shall be hidden in the earth"], a:0, ref:"Micah 1:7",verse:"And all the graven images thereof shall be beaten to pieces, and all the hires thereof shall be burned with the fire, and all the idols thereof will I lay desolate: for she gathered it of the hire of an harlot, and they shall return to the hire of an harlot.", insight:"Idols always end as rubble; what men worship, God breaks."},
{q:"What is meant by 'the hire of an harlot'?", options:["Her wealth was gained through idolatry, and would return to idolatry","Her fields were rented to travelers","Her kings paid tribute to Assyria","Her merchants traded with Tyre"], a:0, ref:"Micah 1:7",verse:"And all the graven images thereof shall be beaten to pieces, and all the hires thereof shall be burned with the fire, and all the idols thereof will I lay desolate: for she gathered it of the hire of an harlot, and they shall return to the hire of an harlot.", insight:"Gain that comes from turning from God never stays; it returns to the sin that made it."},
{q:"How does Micah answer the coming judgment?", options:["He will wail and howl, and go stripped and naked","He will flee to Egypt","He will sing songs of triumph","He will close his mouth in silence"], a:0, ref:"Micah 1:8",verse:"Therefore I will wail and howl, I will go stripped and naked: I will make a wailing like the dragons, and mourning as the owls.", insight:"The true prophet grieves over the judgment he must speak; tears are the right answer to ruin."},
{q:"How far has the wound come?", options:["Unto Judah, even to the gate of my people, even to Jerusalem","Only to the borders of Samaria","As far as the river Euphrates","Into the wilderness of Edom"], a:0, ref:"Micah 1:9",verse:"For her wound is incurable; for it is come unto Judah; he is come unto the gate of my people, even to Jerusalem.", insight:"Sin's wound travels; what begins in Samaria knocks at Jerusalem's gate."},
{q:"What are they told not to do at Gath?", options:["Declare it not at Gath, weep ye not at all","Build no altars at Gath","Send no messengers to Gath","Buy no fields in Gath"], a:0, ref:"Micah 1:10",verse:"Declare ye it not at Gath, weep ye not at all: in the house of Aphrah roll thyself in the dust.", insight:"Do not give the enemies of God cause to rejoice; some griefs are too sacred for the talk of Gath."},
{q:"What should the house of Aphrah do?", options:["Roll thyself in the dust","Flee to the mountains","Hide in the caves","Raise an army"], a:0, ref:"Micah 1:10",verse:"Declare ye it not at Gath, weep ye not at all: in the house of Aphrah roll thyself in the dust.", insight:"Aphrah's name sounds like dust, and dust is her answer; when judgment falls, humility is the only hiding place."},
{q:"What did the inhabitant of Maroth wait for, and what came?", options:["Waited carefully for good, but evil came down from the LORD","Waited for the harvest, but the locusts came","Waited for the king, but the king fled","Waited for rain, but drought came"], a:0, ref:"Micah 1:12",verse:"For the inhabitant of Maroth waited carefully for good: but evil came down from the LORD unto the gate of Jerusalem.", insight:"Waiting for good while walking in evil ends in disappointment; God will not bless what He has condemned."},
{q:"Why must Lachish bind the chariot to the swift beast?", options:["She is the beginning of the sin to the daughter of Zion","She is the last city of Judah","She has the fastest horses in the land","She must carry the ark to safety"], a:0, ref:"Micah 1:13",verse:"O thou inhabitant of Lachish, bind the chariot to the swift beast: she is the beginning of the sin to the daughter of Zion: for the transgressions of Israel were found in thee.", insight:"Lachish led Judah into idolatry; those who pioneer sin become its chief examples."},
{q:"What will the houses of Achzib be?", options:["A lie to the kings of Israel","A fortress for Judah","A temple of the LORD","A market of the nations"], a:0, ref:"Micah 1:14",verse:"Therefore shalt thou give presents to Moresheth-gath: the houses of Achzib shall be a lie to the kings of Israel.", insight:"Achzib's name means deception, and deception is all she proves to be; false hopes fail when kings need them most."},
{q:"What will come to the inhabitant of Mareshah?", options:["An heir, who shall come unto Adullam, the glory of Israel","A prophet with glad tidings","A king to restore the walls","A priest to cleanse the land"], a:0, ref:"Micah 1:15",verse:"Yet will I bring an heir unto thee, O inhabitant of Mareshah: he shall come unto Adullam the glory of Israel.", insight:"An heir here is an invader who inherits the city; God's judgments keep their promises."},
{q:"What will happen to the delicate children?", options:["They are gone into captivity","They are hidden in the hills","They are adopted by the king","They are sent to Egypt"], a:0, ref:"Micah 1:16",verse:"Make thee bald, and poll thee for thy delicate children; enlarge thy baldness as the eagle; for they are gone into captivity from thee.", insight:"Judgment takes the tenderest first; that is why the prophet weeps."}
]},
{n:2, name:"Woe to the Night Plotters", seal:{ref:"Micah 2:11",verse:"If a man walking in the spirit and falsehood do lie, saying, I will prophesy unto thee of wine and of strong drink; he shall even be the prophet of this people."}, facts:["Did you know 'casting a cord by lot' (Micah 2:5) was how land in Israel was measured out and divided by lot, so losing it meant losing your family's place among God's people forever?","Did you know Bozrah, where God will gather His remnant 'as the sheep of Bozrah' (Micah 2:12), was a famous sheep raising region, and its name became a picture of one vast, noisy flock?","Did you know Micah 2:13's 'breaker' going up before the flock pictures a ram breaking through the sheepfold gate, with their king, and the LORD Himself, leading the way out?"], questions:[
{q:"When do the wicked devise iniquity?", options:["Upon their beds, in the night","In the temple courts","At the city gates","On the battlefield"], a:0, ref:"Micah 2:1",verse:"Woe to them that devise iniquity, and work evil upon their beds! when the morning is light, they practise it, because it is in the power of their hand.", insight:"Sin plans at night what it practices by day; the schemer's bed is his first workshop."},
{q:"When do they carry out their evil plans?", options:["When the morning is light","At the midnight hour","On the sabbath day","In the secret chamber"], a:0, ref:"Micah 2:1",verse:"Woe to them that devise iniquity, and work evil upon their beds! when the morning is light, they practise it, because it is in the power of their hand.", insight:"They wait for daylight to do darkness; boldness in evil is still evil."},
{q:"What do the oppressors covet?", options:["Fields and houses","Gold and silver","Horses and chariots","Crowns and thrones"], a:0, ref:"Micah 2:2",verse:"And they covet fields, and take them by violence; and houses, and take them away: so they oppress a man and his house, even a man and his heritage.", insight:"Covetousness is theft before the fact; the wanting is already the wound."},
{q:"How do they take what they covet?", options:["By violence","By fair purchase","By royal gift","By honest labor"], a:0, ref:"Micah 2:2",verse:"And they covet fields, and take them by violence; and houses, and take them away: so they oppress a man and his house, even a man and his heritage.", insight:"Power that takes by violence is robbery with a title; God calls it what it is."},
{q:"What does the LORD say He will devise against this family?", options:["An evil, from which they shall not remove their necks","A blessing for their houses","A famine for their fields","A plague for their cattle"], a:0, ref:"Micah 2:3",verse:"Therefore thus saith the LORD; Behold, against this family do I devise an evil, from which ye shall not remove your necks; neither shall ye go haughtily: for this time is evil.", insight:"They plan evil against their neighbors; God plans the reckoning. No neck is too proud to bow when He lays on the yoke."},
{q:"What cry will they lift in that day?", options:["We be utterly spoiled","Blessed be the LORD","Peace at last","The LORD has forgotten us"], a:0, ref:"Micah 2:4",verse:"In that day shall one take up a parable against you, and lament with a doleful lamentation, and say, We be utterly spoiled: he hath changed the portion of my people: how hath he removed it from me! turning away he hath divided our fields.", insight:"The spoiler will be spoiled; those who divided others' fields will weep over their own."},
{q:"What will they have none of in the congregation of the LORD?", options:["None that shall cast a cord by lot","None that shall offer sacrifice","None that shall sing psalms","None that shall keep the feasts"], a:0, ref:"Micah 2:5",verse:"Therefore thou shalt have none that shall cast a cord by lot in the congregation of the LORD.", insight:"To lose your measured lot is to lose your place among God's people; stolen land forfeits the inheritance."},
{q:"What do the people say to the prophets?", options:["Prophesy ye not","Speak only of peace","Tell us smooth things","Bless our houses"], a:0, ref:"Micah 2:6",verse:"Prophesy ye not, say they to them that prophesy: they shall not prophesy to them, that they shall not take shame.", insight:"When the message stings, men silence the messenger; but silenced prophets do not silence God."},
{q:"What does God ask about His own words?", options:["Do not my words do good to him that walketh uprightly?","Have my words failed forever?","Are my words too hard for men?","Have my words been forgotten?"], a:0, ref:"Micah 2:7",verse:"O thou that art named the house of Jacob, is the spirit of the LORD straitened? are these his doings? do not my words do good to him that walketh uprightly?", insight:"The upright find God's words good; the same sun that softens wax hardens clay."},
{q:"How has God's people risen up of late?", options:["As an enemy","As a mighty army","As a holy nation","As a quiet remnant"], a:0, ref:"Micah 2:8",verse:"Even of late my people is risen up as an enemy: ye pull off the robe with the garment from them that pass by securely as men averse from war.", insight:"God's own people acting as His enemy: that is the deepest wound a nation can give Him."},
{q:"What do they strip from those who pass by securely?", options:["The robe with the garment","Their sandals and staff","Their bread and water","Their inheritance of land"], a:0, ref:"Micah 2:8",verse:"Even of late my people is risen up as an enemy: ye pull off the robe with the garment from them that pass by securely as men averse from war.", insight:"Robbing the peaceful traveler is cowardice dressed as courage; God sees the highwayman in the well dressed."},
{q:"What did they do to the women of God's people?", options:["Cast them out from their pleasant houses","Sold them into Egypt","Drove them to the wilderness","Shut them in the prisons"], a:0, ref:"Micah 2:9",verse:"The women of my people have ye cast out from their pleasant houses; from their children have ye taken away my glory for ever.", insight:"They broke up homes and called it business; God keeps the account of every evicted household."},
{q:"What did they take away from the children?", options:["My glory, for ever","Their daily bread","Their parents' blessing","Their portion of land"], a:0, ref:"Micah 2:9",verse:"The women of my people have ye cast out from their pleasant houses; from their children have ye taken away my glory for ever.", insight:"To rob children of God's glory is the cruelest theft; what is taken from the young echoes forever."},
{q:"What is the command, and why?", options:["Arise ye, and depart; for this is not your rest","Stay and rebuild the walls","Flee to Egypt for safety","Hide in the mountains"], a:0, ref:"Micah 2:10",verse:"Arise ye, and depart; for this is not your rest: because it is polluted, it shall destroy you, even with a sore destruction.", insight:"This world is not our rest; when a land is polluted by sin, God's people must loosen their grip on it."},
{q:"Why will the land destroy them?", options:["Because it is polluted, it shall destroy you, even with a sore destruction","Because the harvest failed","Because the Assyrians are strong","Because the walls are broken"], a:0, ref:"Micah 2:10",verse:"Arise ye, and depart; for this is not your rest: because it is polluted, it shall destroy you, even with a sore destruction.", insight:"Polluted ground cannot hold God's people; sin poisons the very soil of home."},
{q:"What would the people gladly hear prophesied?", options:["Wine and strong drink","War and judgment","Repentance and fasting","Exile and return"], a:0, ref:"Micah 2:11",verse:"If a man walking in the spirit and falsehood do lie, saying, I will prophesy unto thee of wine and of strong drink; he shall even be the prophet of this people.", insight:"A lying prophet with a pleasant message will always find a crowd; popularity is no proof of truth."},
{q:"Whom will the LORD surely gather?", options:["The remnant of Israel","The armies of Assyria","The merchants of Tyre","The priests of Bethel"], a:0, ref:"Micah 2:12",verse:"I will surely assemble, O Jacob, all of thee; I will surely gather the remnant of Israel; I will put them together as the sheep of Bozrah, as the flock in the midst of their fold: they shall make great noise by reason of the multitude of men.", insight:"After judgment, gathering; God never finishes with scattering. A remnant is His specialty."},
{q:"As what will He put them together?", options:["As the sheep of Bozrah, as the flock in the midst of their fold","As stars in the firmament","As trees in the forest","As stones in the wall"], a:0, ref:"Micah 2:12",verse:"I will surely assemble, O Jacob, all of thee; I will surely gather the remnant of Israel; I will put them together as the sheep of Bozrah, as the flock in the midst of their fold: they shall make great noise by reason of the multitude of men.", insight:"The Shepherd gathers His scattered sheep; Bozrah's crowded fold is the picture of God's restoring care."},
{q:"Who has gone up before them?", options:["The breaker","The king of Assyria","A hired guide","The high priest"], a:0, ref:"Micah 2:13",verse:"The breaker is come up before them: they have broken up, and have passed through the gate, and are gone out by it: and their king shall pass before them, and the LORD on the head of them.", insight:"The Breaker goes first through the gate; the promised King opens the way His flock will follow."},
{q:"Who shall pass before them?", options:["Their king, and the LORD on the head of them","The Assyrian captains","The elders of the city","The merchants with their goods"], a:0, ref:"Micah 2:13",verse:"The breaker is come up before them: they have broken up, and have passed through the gate, and are gone out by it: and their king shall pass before them, and the LORD on the head of them.", insight:"The King Himself leads the march; when the LORD is at the head, the gate cannot hold."}
]},
{n:3, name:"The Leaders Who Sold Justice", seal:{ref:"Micah 3:12",verse:"Therefore shall Zion for your sake be plowed as a field, and Jerusalem shall become heaps, and the mountain of the house as the high places of the forest."}, facts:["Did you know Micah's charge that the leaders 'build up Zion with blood' (Micah 3:10) means their grand building projects were paid for by oppression, and God counted every brick?","Did you know Micah 3:12, 'Zion shall be plowed as a field,' was quoted a century later by the elders defending Jeremiah, proof that a true prophecy outlives its prophet (Jeremiah 26:18)?","Did you know 'cover their lips' (Micah 3:7) pictures the mourning veil, so the shamed seers wear grief as their uniform when God gives no answer?"], questions:[
{q:"To whom does Micah speak in this chapter?", options:["The heads of Jacob, and the princes of the house of Israel","The farmers of the field","The children in the streets","The shepherds of the flock"], a:0, ref:"Micah 3:1",verse:"And I said, Hear, I pray you, O heads of Jacob, and ye princes of the house of Israel; Is it not for you to know judgment?", insight:"The word aims at the top; when leaders rot, the prophet speaks to the head of the house first."},
{q:"What is it for the rulers to know?", options:["Judgment","The law of Moses by heart","The art of war","The trade of the nations"], a:0, ref:"Micah 3:1",verse:"And I said, Hear, I pray you, O heads of Jacob, and ye princes of the house of Israel; Is it not for you to know judgment?", insight:"Rulers are appointed to know judgment; ignorance of right is no excuse in a judge."},
{q:"What do the corrupt rulers hate and love?", options:["They hate the good, and love the evil","They hate the poor, and love the rich","They hate the temple, and love the palace","They hate the prophets, and love the priests"], a:0, ref:"Micah 3:2",verse:"Who hate the good, and love the evil; who pluck off their skin from off them, and their flesh from off their bones;", insight:"Hating good and loving evil is the exact upside down of righteousness; check what your own heart loves."},
{q:"What do they pluck off the people?", options:["Their skin from off them, and their flesh from off their bones","Their robes and sandals","Their rings and bracelets","Their houses and lands"], a:0, ref:"Micah 3:2",verse:"Who hate the good, and love the evil; who pluck off their skin from off them, and their flesh from off their bones;", insight:"Oppression is described as butchery; God sees greedy rulers as devourers of their own people."},
{q:"How do the rulers treat God's people?", options:["As flesh chopped in pieces for the pot and the caldron","As sheep led to green pasture","As guests at a rich feast","As servants in the palace"], a:0, ref:"Micah 3:3",verse:"Who also eat the flesh of my people, and flay their skin from off them; and they break their bones, and chop them in pieces, as for the pot, and as flesh within the caldron.", insight:"Men reduced to meat in a pot; that is how heaven views the abuse of power."},
{q:"What will happen when they cry unto the LORD?", options:["He will not hear them, but hide his face from them","He will answer them speedily","He will send them a prophet","He will forgive them at once"], a:0, ref:"Micah 3:4",verse:"Then shall they cry unto the LORD, but he will not hear them: he will even hide his face from them at that time, as they have behaved themselves ill in their doings.", insight:"There is a time when God stops listening; mercy refused hardens into judgment."},
{q:"Why will He hide His face from them?", options:["As they have behaved themselves ill in their doings","Because He has forgotten them","Because the temple is destroyed","Because the priests are few"], a:0, ref:"Micah 3:4",verse:"Then shall they cry unto the LORD, but he will not hear them: he will even hide his face from them at that time, as they have behaved themselves ill in their doings.", insight:"God turns His face as men turned their backs; His silence answers their conduct."},
{q:"What do the false prophets cry?", options:["Peace","War","Famine","Exile"], a:0, ref:"Micah 3:5",verse:"Thus saith the LORD concerning the prophets that make my people err, that bite with their teeth, and cry, Peace; and he that putteth not into their mouths, they even prepare war against him.", insight:"Peace on the lips of a hireling is a lullaby for the doomed; true peace never flatters sin."},
{q:"Against whom do they prepare war?", options:["Him that putteth not into their mouths","The king of Assyria","The true prophets of God","The elders of Israel"], a:0, ref:"Micah 3:5",verse:"Thus saith the LORD concerning the prophets that make my people err, that bite with their teeth, and cry, Peace; and he that putteth not into their mouths, they even prepare war against him.", insight:"Their message is for sale; no pay, no peace. Beware the preacher whose blessing has a price."},
{q:"What will become of the prophets' visions?", options:["Night shall be unto them; they shall have no vision","They shall see clearer than ever","They shall dream dreams of glory","They shall prophesy to the nations"], a:0, ref:"Micah 3:6",verse:"Therefore night shall be unto you, that ye shall not have a vision; and it shall be dark unto you, that ye shall not divine; and the sun shall go down over the prophets, and the day shall be dark over them.", insight:"God can shut the heavens over a lying prophet; no vision comes to those who sold the truth."},
{q:"What shall the sun do over the prophets?", options:["Go down over them, and the day shall be dark","Rise with healing in its wings","Shine seven times brighter","Stand still at noon"], a:0, ref:"Micah 3:6",verse:"Therefore night shall be unto you, that ye shall not have a vision; and it shall be dark unto you, that ye shall not divine; and the sun shall go down over the prophets, and the day shall be dark over them.", insight:"Their day ends in darkness; a ministry built on flattery sets like a sun that will not rise."},
{q:"Why will the seers cover their lips?", options:["For there is no answer of God","For the king commands silence","For the people have fled","For the temple is shut"], a:0, ref:"Micah 3:7",verse:"Then shall the seers be ashamed, and the diviners confounded: yea, they shall all cover their lips; for there is no answer of God.", insight:"Shame covers the mouth that lied; when God gives no answer, the diviner's craft is exposed."},
{q:"What will happen to the seers and the diviners?", options:["The seers shall be ashamed, and the diviners confounded","The seers shall dream new dreams","The diviners shall be honored by the king","The seers shall flee to Egypt"], a:0, ref:"Micah 3:7",verse:"Then shall the seers be ashamed, and the diviners confounded: yea, they shall all cover their lips; for there is no answer of God.", insight:"Ashamed seers and confounded diviners: a lying ministry ends in public disgrace."},
{q:"With what is Micah full?", options:["With power by the Spirit of the LORD, and with judgment and might","With silver and gold","With dreams and visions","With the wisdom of Egypt"], a:0, ref:"Micah 3:8",verse:"But truly I am full of power by the spirit of the LORD, and of judgment, and of might, to declare unto Jacob his transgression, and to Israel his sin.", insight:"The difference between Micah and the hirelings is the Spirit; boldness to confront sin is heaven's gift."},
{q:"For what purpose is Micah filled with power?", options:["To declare unto Jacob his transgression, and to Israel his sin","To bless the kings of Judah","To comfort the afflicted only","To sing in the temple"], a:0, ref:"Micah 3:8",verse:"But truly I am full of power by the spirit of the LORD, and of judgment, and of might, to declare unto Jacob his transgression, and to Israel his sin.", insight:"The Spirit's power is given to name sin plainly; comfort without conviction is not the Spirit's work."},
{q:"What do the rulers abhor?", options:["Judgment","The prophets","The poor","The temple"], a:0, ref:"Micah 3:9",verse:"Hear this, I pray you, ye heads of the house of Jacob, and princes of the house of Israel, that abhor judgment, and pervert all equity.", insight:"Abhorring judgment while sitting in judgment: that is the corruption Micah names."},
{q:"How do they build up Zion?", options:["With blood, and Jerusalem with iniquity","With cedar and gold","With prayer and fasting","With the labor of volunteers"], a:0, ref:"Micah 3:10",verse:"They build up Zion with blood, and Jerusalem with iniquity.", insight:"Grand projects built on blood are an abomination; God does not admire architecture paid for in injustice."},
{q:"Why do the heads judge, the priests teach, and the prophets divine?", options:["For reward, for hire, and for money","For the glory of God","For the love of the people","For the honor of the temple"], a:0, ref:"Micah 3:11",verse:"The heads thereof judge for reward, and the priests thereof teach for hire, and the prophets thereof divine for money: yet will they lean upon the LORD, and say, Is not the LORD among us? none evil can come upon us.", insight:"Justice for sale, teaching for hire, prophecy for money; when ministry becomes merchandise, judgment is near."},
{q:"What do these corrupt leaders claim?", options:["Is not the LORD among us? none evil can come upon us","The LORD has forsaken us","We are too sinful to be saved","The prophets have deceived us"], a:0, ref:"Micah 3:11",verse:"The heads thereof judge for reward, and the priests thereof teach for hire, and the prophets thereof divine for money: yet will they lean upon the LORD, and say, Is not the LORD among us? none evil can come upon us.", insight:"The LORD is among us, on the lips of the corrupt, is presumption, not faith; God's presence is no shield for rebellion."},
{q:"What shall Zion and Jerusalem become for their sake?", options:["Zion plowed as a field, and Jerusalem heaps","Zion a garden of delight, and Jerusalem a praise","Zion a holy mountain, and Jerusalem a refuge","Zion a quiet habitation, and Jerusalem a joy"], a:0, ref:"Micah 3:12",verse:"Therefore shall Zion for your sake be plowed as a field, and Jerusalem shall become heaps, and the mountain of the house as the high places of the forest.", insight:"The holy city plowed like a common field; no place is so sacred that sin cannot forfeit it."}
]},
{n:4, name:"Swords into Plowshares", seal:{ref:"Micah 4:3",verse:"And he shall judge among many people, and rebuke strong nations afar off; and they shall beat their swords into plowshares, and their spears into pruninghooks: nation shall not lift up a sword against nation, neither shall they learn war any more."}, facts:["Did you know 'swords into plowshares' (Micah 4:3) is engraved on a wall at the United Nations headquarters in New York, quoted from this very chapter?","Did you know 'every man under his vine and under his fig tree' (Micah 4:4) was the Bible's favorite picture of peace and plenty, used for Solomon's golden age in 1 Kings 4:25?","Did you know Micah names Babylon as the place of exile (Micah 4:10) more than a century before Babylon rose to power, and in the same breath promises deliverance there?"], questions:[
{q:"When shall the mountain of the house of the LORD be exalted?", options:["In the last days","In the days of Hezekiah","In the year of Jubilee","At the next new moon"], a:0, ref:"Micah 4:1",verse:"But in the last days it shall come to pass, that the mountain of the house of the LORD shall be established in the top of the mountains, and it shall be exalted above the hills; and people shall flow unto it.", insight:"God's best is kept for the last days; hope always looks forward, never back."},
{q:"What will the people do toward the exalted mountain?", options:["People shall flow unto it","Armies shall march against it","Merchants shall trade upon it","Kings shall tax it"], a:0, ref:"Micah 4:1",verse:"But in the last days it shall come to pass, that the mountain of the house of the LORD shall be established in the top of the mountains, and it shall be exalted above the hills; and people shall flow unto it.", insight:"People shall flow unto it like rivers to the sea; when God lifts His house, hearts stream toward it."},
{q:"What shall go forth of Zion?", options:["The law, and the word of the LORD from Jerusalem","Armies to conquer the nations","Tribute to the kings of the earth","Merchants to every land"], a:0, ref:"Micah 4:2",verse:"And many nations shall come, and say, Come, and let us go up to the mountain of the LORD, and to the house of the God of Jacob; and he will teach us of his ways, and we will walk in his paths: for the law shall go forth of Zion, and the word of the LORD from Jerusalem.", insight:"Zion's export is the word of God; the law going forth is greater than any army marching out."},
{q:"What will the nations do with their swords, and what will they no longer learn?", options:["Beat them into plowshares, and learn war no more","Hang them in the temple, and learn trade instead","Bury them in the desert, and learn farming","Melt them into idols, and learn worship"], a:0, ref:"Micah 4:3",verse:"And he shall judge among many people, and rebuke strong nations afar off; and they shall beat their swords into plowshares, and their spears into pruninghooks: nation shall not lift up a sword against nation, neither shall they learn war any more.", insight:"Weapons become farm tools when the promised King reigns; war is not eternal, but peace will be."},
{q:"What is the picture of peace in that day?", options:["Every man under his vine and under his fig tree","Every man in his chariot of war","Every man behind his city wall","Every man with his sword at rest"], a:0, ref:"Micah 4:4",verse:"But they shall sit every man under his vine and under his fig tree; and none shall make them afraid: for the mouth of the LORD of hosts hath spoken it.", insight:"A vine and a fig tree: peace you can sit under. God's rest is not abstract; it has shade."},
{q:"Why is this peace certain?", options:["For the mouth of the LORD of hosts hath spoken it","For the kings have signed a treaty","For the armies are too tired to fight","For the walls are strong"], a:0, ref:"Micah 4:4",verse:"But they shall sit every man under his vine and under his fig tree; and none shall make them afraid: for the mouth of the LORD of hosts hath spoken it.", insight:"The mouth of the LORD has spoken it; when God says peace, no power can unsay it."},
{q:"In whose name will we walk?", options:["In the name of the LORD our God for ever and ever","In the name of our kings","In the name of our fathers","In the name of the nations"], a:0, ref:"Micah 4:5",verse:"For all people will walk every one in the name of his god, and we will walk in the name of the LORD our God for ever and ever.", insight:"Others walk in the name of their gods; we walk in the name of the LORD, for ever and ever. Allegiance is the heart of worship."},
{q:"Whom will the LORD assemble in that day?", options:["Her that halteth","The mighty warriors","The rich merchants","The foreign kings"], a:0, ref:"Micah 4:6",verse:"In that day, saith the LORD, will I assemble her that halteth, and I will gather her that is driven out, and her that I have afflicted;", insight:"He assembles her that halteth; the lame are first on God's guest list for the kingdom."},
{q:"Whom will He gather besides?", options:["Her that is driven out, and her that He has afflicted","The armies of the east","The sailors of the sea","The builders of the wall"], a:0, ref:"Micah 4:6",verse:"In that day, saith the LORD, will I assemble her that halteth, and I will gather her that is driven out, and her that I have afflicted;", insight:"The driven out and the afflicted are gathered by the same hand that scattered them; God's discipline ends in embrace."},
{q:"What will her that halted become?", options:["A remnant","A great army","A royal priesthood","A walled city"], a:0, ref:"Micah 4:7",verse:"And I will make her that halted a remnant, and her that was cast far off a strong nation: and the LORD shall reign over them in mount Zion from henceforth, even for ever.", insight:"The halted become the remnant; God builds His future out of the broken."},
{q:"What will her that was cast far off become?", options:["A strong nation","A tributary province","A desert waste","A forgotten tribe"], a:0, ref:"Micah 4:7",verse:"And I will make her that halted a remnant, and her that was cast far off a strong nation: and the LORD shall reign over them in mount Zion from henceforth, even for ever.", insight:"Cast far off, made a strong nation; distance from home is no distance from God's purpose."},
{q:"What shall come to the daughter of Jerusalem?", options:["The kingdom, even the first dominion","Tribute from the nations","A new temple of gold","An everlasting covenant of peace"], a:0, ref:"Micah 4:8",verse:"And thou, O tower of the flock, the strong hold of the daughter of Zion, unto thee shall it come, even the first dominion; the kingdom shall come to the daughter of Jerusalem.", insight:"The kingdom shall come; God's rule returns to Zion, and this time it stays forever."},
{q:"What pangs have taken her?", options:["Pangs as of a woman in travail","Pangs of hunger and thirst","Pangs of a wounded soldier","Pangs of a grieving mother"], a:0, ref:"Micah 4:9",verse:"Now why dost thou cry out aloud? is there no king in thee? is thy counsellor perished? for pangs have taken thee as a woman in travail.", insight:"Travail pangs come before the birth; the pain of the present is the promise of what is coming."},
{q:"Where must the daughter of Zion go?", options:["Even to Babylon","To Egypt","To Assyria","To the wilderness"], a:0, ref:"Micah 4:10",verse:"Be in pain, and labour to bring forth, O daughter of Zion, like a woman in travail: for now shalt thou go forth out of the city, and thou shalt dwell in the field, and thou shalt go even to Babylon; there shalt thou be delivered; there the LORD shall redeem thee from the hand of thine enemies.", insight:"The road to deliverance runs through Babylon; God often redeems us in the very place of our exile."},
{q:"What will happen to her there?", options:["There shall she be delivered; the LORD shall redeem her","There shall she perish utterly","There shall she serve idols","There shall she be forgotten"], a:0, ref:"Micah 4:10",verse:"Be in pain, and labour to bring forth, O daughter of Zion, like a woman in travail: for now shalt thou go forth out of the city, and thou shalt dwell in the field, and thou shalt go even to Babylon; there shalt thou be delivered; there the LORD shall redeem thee from the hand of thine enemies.", insight:"There shalt thou be delivered; the darkest address becomes the place of rescue when the LORD is there."},
{q:"What do the gathered nations say?", options:["Let her be defiled, and let our eye look upon Zion","Let her be blessed above all cities","Let us go up and worship with her","Let us make a covenant with her"], a:0, ref:"Micah 4:11",verse:"Now also many nations are gathered against thee, that say, Let her be defiled, and let our eye look upon Zion.", insight:"The nations gather to gloat; they do not know they are gathering for their own judgment."},
{q:"What do the nations not know?", options:["The thoughts of the LORD, neither understand His counsel","The number of their armies","The strength of Zion's walls","The name of Zion's king"], a:0, ref:"Micah 4:12",verse:"But they know not the thoughts of the LORD, neither understand they his counsel: for he shall gather them as the sheaves into the floor.", insight:"They know not the thoughts of the LORD; the world's wisdom cannot read God's mind."},
{q:"As what will He gather them?", options:["As the sheaves into the floor","As sheep into the fold","As water into the sea","As stars into the sky"], a:0, ref:"Micah 4:12",verse:"But they know not the thoughts of the LORD, neither understand they his counsel: for he shall gather them as the sheaves into the floor.", insight:"Gathered as sheaves for the threshing floor; the nations assemble for harvest, and the harvest is judgment."},
{q:"What will her horn and her hoofs be made?", options:["Her horn iron, and her hoofs brass","Her horn silver, and her hoofs gold","Her horn wood, and her hoofs clay","Her horn bronze, and her hoofs stone"], a:0, ref:"Micah 4:13",verse:"Arise and thresh, O daughter of Zion: for I will make thine horn iron, and I will make thy hoofs brass: and thou shalt beat in pieces many people: and I will consecrate their gain unto the LORD, and their substance unto the Lord of the whole earth.", insight:"Iron horn and brass hoofs: God arms the weak for the threshing He appoints them."},
{q:"To whom will their gain be consecrated?", options:["Unto the LORD, and their substance unto the Lord of the whole earth","Unto the king of Babylon","Unto the priests of the temple","Unto the poor of the land"], a:0, ref:"Micah 4:13",verse:"Arise and thresh, O daughter of Zion: for I will make thine horn iron, and I will make thy hoofs brass: and thou shalt beat in pieces many people: and I will consecrate their gain unto the LORD, and their substance unto the Lord of the whole earth.", insight:"The spoil of the nations belongs to the Lord of the whole earth; every victory is His tribute."}
]},
{n:5, name:"The Ruler from Bethlehem", seal:{ref:"Micah 5:2",verse:"But thou, Bethlehem Ephratah, though thou be little among the thousands of Judah, yet out of thee shall he come forth unto me that is to be ruler in Israel; whose goings forth have been from of old, from everlasting."}, facts:["Did you know Micah 5:2's promise of a ruler from Bethlehem was quoted by the chief priests to Herod when the wise men asked where Christ would be born (Matthew 2:5-6)?","Did you know Bethlehem means 'house of bread,' and Ephratah, the old clan name, marks this Bethlehem in Judah apart from another Bethlehem in the north?","Did you know 'the land of Nimrod' (Micah 5:6) reaches back to Genesis 10, where Nimrod the mighty hunter founded the first cities of Assyria and Babylon?"], questions:[
{q:"What is laid against us?", options:["Siege","A feast","A tribute","A blessing"], a:0, ref:"Micah 5:1",verse:"Now gather thyself in troops, O daughter of troops: he hath laid siege against us: they shall smite the judge of Israel with a rod upon the cheek.", insight:"Siege is laid, but God is not surprised; the enemy's plans are the stage for His deliverance."},
{q:"What shall they do to the judge of Israel?", options:["Smite him with a rod upon the cheek","Crown him with gold","Set him on a throne","Anoint him with oil"], a:0, ref:"Micah 5:1",verse:"Now gather thyself in troops, O daughter of troops: he hath laid siege against us: they shall smite the judge of Israel with a rod upon the cheek.", insight:"The judge smitten on the cheek: Israel's ruler humiliated. Yet out of humiliation, God raises the true King."},
{q:"From which little town shall the ruler come forth, whose goings forth are from everlasting?", options:["Bethlehem Ephratah","Jerusalem","Hebron","Nazareth"], a:0, ref:"Micah 5:2",verse:"But thou, Bethlehem Ephratah, though thou be little among the thousands of Judah, yet out of thee shall he come forth unto me that is to be ruler in Israel; whose goings forth have been from of old, from everlasting.", insight:"Bethlehem, little among the thousands of Judah, chosen for the greatest birth; God delights to use the small, and this ruler existed before time."},
{q:"Until when will He give them up?", options:["Until the time that she which travaileth hath brought forth","Until the walls are rebuilt","Until the temple falls","Until the stars fall"], a:0, ref:"Micah 5:3",verse:"Therefore will he give them up, until the time that she which travaileth hath brought forth: then the remnant of his brethren shall return unto the children of Israel.", insight:"Abandonment with an expiration date; God gives up His people only until the promised birth."},
{q:"In what strength shall He feed His flock?", options:["In the strength of the LORD, in the majesty of the name of the LORD his God","In the strength of horses and chariots","In the strength of walled cities","In the strength of many counselors"], a:0, ref:"Micah 5:4",verse:"And he shall stand and feed in the strength of the LORD, in the majesty of the name of the LORD his God; and they shall abide: for now shall he be great unto the ends of the earth.", insight:"He feeds in the strength of the LORD; the Shepherd is strong because His God is strong."},
{q:"How great shall He be?", options:["Great unto the ends of the earth","Great in Jerusalem only","Great among the shepherds","Great for a hundred years"], a:0, ref:"Micah 5:4",verse:"And he shall stand and feed in the strength of the LORD, in the majesty of the name of the LORD his God; and they shall abide: for now shall he be great unto the ends of the earth.", insight:"Unto the ends of the earth; no border limits this greatness."},
{q:"Who shall be the peace?", options:["This man","The king of Assyria","The high priest","The elders of Judah"], a:0, ref:"Micah 5:5",verse:"And this man shall be the peace, when the Assyrian shall come into our land: and when he shall tread in our palaces, then shall we raise against him seven shepherds, and eight principal men.", insight:"This man shall be the peace; peace is not a treaty but a Person."},
{q:"How many shepherds and principal men shall be raised against the Assyrian?", options:["Seven shepherds, and eight principal men","Three shepherds, and four princes","Twelve shepherds, and twelve princes","One shepherd, and one prince"], a:0, ref:"Micah 5:5",verse:"And this man shall be the peace, when the Assyrian shall come into our land: and when he shall tread in our palaces, then shall we raise against him seven shepherds, and eight principal men.", insight:"Seven and eight: completeness upon completeness; God's defense is more than enough."},
{q:"What is the land of Assyria also called?", options:["The land of Nimrod","The land of giants","The land of darkness","The land of the east"], a:0, ref:"Micah 5:6",verse:"And they shall waste the land of Assyria with the sword, and the land of Nimrod in the entrances thereof: thus shall he deliver us from the Assyrian, when he cometh into our land, and when he treadeth within our borders.", insight:"Nimrod, the first empire builder of Genesis 10; every proud empire since is only his echo."},
{q:"From whom shall He deliver us?", options:["From the Assyrian, when he cometh into our land","From the famine in the land","From the plague in the city","From the strife among brethren"], a:0, ref:"Micah 5:6",verse:"And they shall waste the land of Assyria with the sword, and the land of Nimrod in the entrances thereof: thus shall he deliver us from the Assyrian, when he cometh into our land, and when he treadeth within our borders.", insight:"He delivers from the Assyrian at our borders; God meets the threat where it treads."},
{q:"As what shall the remnant of Jacob be among the peoples?", options:["As a dew from the LORD, as the showers upon the grass","As a fire among the stubble","As a flood upon the valley","As a storm upon the sea"], a:0, ref:"Micah 5:7",verse:"And the remnant of Jacob shall be in the midst of many people as a dew from the LORD, as the showers upon the grass, that tarrieth not for man, nor waiteth for the sons of men.", insight:"A dew from the LORD: quiet, heaven sent, life giving. God's people bless the world without noise."},
{q:"For whom does the dew wait?", options:["It tarrieth not for man, nor waiteth for the sons of men","It waits for the king's command","It waits for the farmer's prayer","It waits for the appointed season"], a:0, ref:"Micah 5:7",verse:"And the remnant of Jacob shall be in the midst of many people as a dew from the LORD, as the showers upon the grass, that tarrieth not for man, nor waiteth for the sons of men.", insight:"The dew waits for no man; God's refreshing comes on heaven's schedule, not ours."},
{q:"As what else shall the remnant be among the Gentiles?", options:["As a lion among the beasts of the forest","As a dove among the eagles","As a lamb among the wolves","As a deer among the hunters"], a:0, ref:"Micah 5:8",verse:"And the remnant of Jacob shall be among the Gentiles in the midst of many people as a lion among the beasts of the forest, as a young lion among the flocks of sheep: who, if he go through, both treadeth down, and teareth in pieces, and none can deliver.", insight:"Dew and lion in the same breath: gentle to bless, terrible to resist. God's people carry both."},
{q:"What does the lion do when he goes through the flock?", options:["Both treadeth down, and teareth in pieces, and none can deliver","Roars and scares them far away","Guards them safely through the night","Leads them gently to pasture"], a:0, ref:"Micah 5:8",verse:"And the remnant of Jacob shall be among the Gentiles in the midst of many people as a lion among the beasts of the forest, as a young lion among the flocks of sheep: who, if he go through, both treadeth down, and teareth in pieces, and none can deliver.", insight:"None can deliver from the lion's path; when God moves in judgment, no power stands."},
{q:"What shall happen to all His enemies?", options:["They shall be cut off","They shall be converted","They shall be scattered to the winds","They shall pay tribute"], a:0, ref:"Micah 5:9",verse:"Thine hand shall be lifted up upon thine adversaries, and all thine enemies shall be cut off.", insight:"Thine hand lifted up, enemies cut off; God finishes what He starts against His foes."},
{q:"What will the LORD cut off and destroy?", options:["Thy horses out of the midst of thee, and thy chariots","Thy vineyards and fields","Thy houses and barns","Thy sons and daughters"], a:0, ref:"Micah 5:10",verse:"And it shall come to pass in that day, saith the LORD, that I will cut off thy horses out of the midst of thee, and I will destroy thy chariots:", insight:"Horses and chariots destroyed: God disarms His people's trust in military might, so they trust in Him."},
{q:"What will He cut off out of their hand?", options:["Witchcrafts, and they shall have no more soothsayers","Their swords and spears","Their plows and pruninghooks","Their silver and gold"], a:0, ref:"Micah 5:12",verse:"And I will cut off witchcrafts out of thine hand; and thou shalt have no more soothsayers:", insight:"Witchcraft and soothsayers cut off; God purges every rival voice so His people hear only Him."},
{q:"What will they no more worship?", options:["The work of their hands","The LORD of hosts","The God of their fathers","The angels of heaven"], a:0, ref:"Micah 5:13",verse:"Thy graven images also will I cut off, and thy standing images out of the midst of thee; and thou shalt no more worship the work of thine hands.", insight:"No more worship of the work of their hands; the creature can never be the Creator."},
{q:"What will He pluck up out of the midst of them?", options:["Thy groves","Thy vineyards","Thy olive trees","Thy cedars"], a:0, ref:"Micah 5:14",verse:"And I will pluck up thy groves out of the midst of thee: so will I destroy thy cities.", insight:"The groves of idolatry plucked up by the roots; God does not prune false worship, He uproots it."},
{q:"Upon whom will He execute vengeance?", options:["Upon the heathen, in anger and fury, such as they have not heard","Upon the house of Jacob","Upon the priests of Levi","Upon the children of Israel"], a:0, ref:"Micah 5:15",verse:"And I will execute vengeance in anger and fury upon the heathen, such as they have not heard.", insight:"Vengeance on the heathen such as they have not heard; God's justice, long delayed, is never denied."}
]}
]);
